---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import JoinBand from '../components/JoinBand.astro';
import HeadFigure from '../components/HeadFigure.astro';
import Emblem from '../components/Emblem.astro';
import { SITE, LINKS } from '../data/site';

const neuroFormats = [
  { t: 'Labs', d: 'Quick experiments you run on yourself, like reaction time and memory tests. Then we compare everyone’s results.' },
  { t: 'Guest speakers', d: 'People who work in medicine and brain science come in, and you get to ask them anything.' },
  { t: 'Journal club', d: 'We read one real research paper and break it down: what they asked, what they did, and what they found.' },
  { t: 'Debates', d: 'Two teams, picked at random, argue a real question about the brain.' },
  { t: 'Brain Bee practice', d: 'The topics that come up most, plus timed practice questions.' },
  { t: 'Brain Awareness Week', d: 'In March we run quick brain science demos for the rest of the school.' },
];
---

<Base title="About" description="How NeuroGIDAS works: one week neuroscience, the next week genetics research. What GIDAS is, and who can join.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap head-grid">
      <div>
        <h1 class="h1">About NeuroGIDAS</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          We’re two clubs in one. One week we learn how the brain works. The next week we do genetics research with real data.
        </p>
      </div>
      <HeadFigure kind="weeks" n={5} />
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <h2 class="h2">How it works</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We meet every Wednesday after school. The weeks switch back and forth between neuroscience and GIDAS. You can come to
          both, or only the one you care about.
        </p>
        <p>
          The two sides connect. Cancer is this year’s research focus, so later in the year we spend time on brain cancer, where
          brain science and genetics overlap.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="trackcard trackcard--neuro">
        <div class="trackcard__head">
          <Emblem variant="neuron" class="trackcard__fig" />
          <div>
            <h2 class="h2">Neuroscience weeks</h2>
            <p class="trackcard__sub">Labs, speakers, and the Brain Bee.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="trackcard__body">
          <p class="trackcard__intro">
            We cover how the brain is built and how it works: neurons, memory, how you see, sleep, and what happens when something
            goes wrong. Most meetings have a short lesson and then something hands-on.
          </p>
          <dl class="formats">
            {
              neuroFormats.map((f) => (
                <div>
                  <dt>{f.t}</dt>
                  <dd>{f.d}</dd>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </dl>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="trackcard trackcard--gidas">
        <div class="trackcard__head">
          <Emblem variant="helix" class="trackcard__fig trackcard__fig--helix" />
          <div>
            <h2 class="h2">GIDAS weeks</h2>
            <p class="trackcard__sub">Genetics research with real data.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="trackcard__body">
          <p class="trackcard__intro">
            GIDAS stands for Genes in Diseases and Symptoms. It’s the high school program of{' '}
            <a href={LINKS.gidas} rel="noopener">miRcore</a>, a nonprofit connected to the University of Michigan with more than
            130 chapters.
          </p>
          <p class="trackcard__intro">
            You start with the basics, like DNA. Then you learn the real tools: NCBI GEO and GEO2R to find genes that change in a
            disease, STRING to see how proteins connect, KEGG to find pathways, and GeneCards, OMIM, Gene Ontology, and the UCSC
            Genome Browser to learn about your genes.
          </p>
          <p class="trackcard__intro">
            You work on one project all year. In April you write it up as an abstract and present it at the miRcore High School
            Research Conference.
          </p>
          <p><a class="link link--light" href="/research/">See each step of the research</a></p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <h2 class="h2">Who can join</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>Anyone at Eastview. You don’t need any experience.</strong> Some people have taken AP Biology, some have
          coded, and plenty have done neither. The first few meetings get everyone caught up.
        </p>
        <p>
          It’s a good fit if you’re curious about medicine, the brain, genetics, or research. Not many high schoolers finish a year
          with their own research question, data they analyzed, and an abstract with their name on it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section rule-top">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <h2 class="h2">When and where</h2>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Day</dt><dd>{SITE.day}, after school</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Time</dt><dd class="tnum">{SITE.time}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Room</dt><dd>{SITE.room}, {SITE.advisor}’s room</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Run by</dt><dd>Co-presidents Aaryav Sharma and Rishik Kondadadi</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <JoinBand />
</Base>

<style>
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: var(--s-6) clamp(2rem, 1rem + 5vw, 6rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .section-tight {
    padding-bottom: var(--section);
  }

  .section-tight .wrap {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-4);
  }

  .trackcard {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: var(--s-6) clamp(2rem, 1rem + 5vw, 6rem);
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 1rem + 3vw, 3.5rem);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    color: #fff;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
  }

  .trackcard--neuro {
    background: var(--indigo);
    --halo: var(--indigo);
  }

  .trackcard--gidas {
    background: var(--teal-ink);
    --halo: var(--teal-ink);
  }

  .trackcard__head {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-5);
    align-content: start;
  }

  .trackcard :global(.trackcard__fig) {
    color: #fff;
    height: 6.5rem;
    width: auto;
  }

  .trackcard :global(.trackcard__fig--helix) {
    height: 8rem;
  }

  .trackcard__sub {
    margin-top: var(--s-2);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82);
  }

  .trackcard__intro {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .trackcard__intro + .trackcard__intro,
  .trackcard__body > p:last-child {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }

  .trackcard a {
    color: #fff;
  }

  .trackcard :focus-visible {
    outline-color: #fff;
  }

  .link--light {
    text-decoration-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
  }

  .formats {
    margin: var(--s-6) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0 var(--s-6);
  }

  .formats div {
    padding: var(--s-4) 0 var(--s-5);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.24);
  }

  .formats dt {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 106;
  }

  .formats dd {
    margin: var(--s-1) 0 0;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82);
  }

  .facts {
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
  }

  .facts div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s-4);
    padding: var(--s-4) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .facts dt {
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .split,
    .trackcard {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .formats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .facts div {
      grid-template-columns: 5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
